      "writtenOn": "2026-06-01T08:28:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: `requestContextProvider.get().getContext()` can return `null` if called outside of a request scope, which would result in a `NullPointerException` when calling `.getUser()`.\n\nYou should check for null before accessing the user:\n\n```java\nRequestContext context \u003d requestContextProvider.get().getContext();\nif (context \u003d\u003d null || !context.getUser().isIdentifiedUser()) {\n  return cachedConfig;\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, you could inject `Provider\u003cCurrentUser\u003e currentUserProvider` instead of getting it from the `RequestContext`. Guice is configured to return an `AnonymousUser` via `FallbackRequestContext` when outside of a request scope, meaning `currentUserProvider.get().isIdentifiedUser()` will safely return `false` without throwing an exception.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 0
      },
